{#
  docker-compose.override.yml — stop the bundled Postgres and MinIO from running.

  WHY THIS FILE EXISTS. Plane's Community compose has NO `profiles`, and plane-db /
  plane-minio carry a hardcoded `replicas: 1` (not templated by an env var), while four
  services `depends_on: plane-db`. So pointing PGHOST/AWS_S3_ENDPOINT_URL at 231/245 is
  NOT enough — `docker compose up` would still start a Postgres and a MinIO on this box,
  quietly holding a second, empty database next to the real one. That is exactly the
  "second unmanaged Postgres" the external-database decision exists to avoid.

  Compose merges override files by default, so the upstream file stays byte-for-byte
  what upstream published and an upgrade remains a one-line version bump.

  ⚠️ VERIFY ON FIRST RUN: `docker compose ps` must show plane-db and plane-minio with
  0 running containers, and `docker compose config` must still resolve. If depends_on
  resolution complains about a zero-scaled service on this Compose version, the fallback
  is to let them run unused — wasteful and confusing, but not harmful.
#}
services:
  plane-db:
    deploy:
      replicas: 0

  plane-minio:
    deploy:
      replicas: 0
